| !JsEdit mode: JavaScript (JSScript files, &F81). See !JsEdit's !Help for the format.
Name       JavaScript
Lexer      c-like
Types      &F81
Indent     2
Comment    //
Block      /* */
Quotes     ' " `
Keywords   async await break case catch class const continue debugger default delete do else export extends
Keywords   finally for from function if import in instanceof let new of return static super switch throw
Keywords   try typeof var void while with yield get set
Constants  true false null undefined NaN Infinity this
Api        task ctx os wimp vfs print input sleep Menu colourMenu wimpColour beep sound saveAs query infoBox
Api        Math JSON Date Number String Array Object console
Functions  ^\s*(?:export\s+)?(?:default\s+)?(?:async\s+)?function\s*\*?\s*([A-Za-z_$][\w$]*)
Functions  ^\s*(?:export\s+)?(?:const|let)\s+([A-Za-z_$][\w$]*)\s*=\s*(?:async\s*)?(?:\([^)]*\)|[A-Za-z_$][\w$]*)\s*=>
Functions  ^\s*([A-Za-z_$][\w$]*)\s*\([^)]*\)\s*\{\s*$
Colour     text 7
Colour     comment 4
Colour     string 13
Colour     number 11
Colour     keyword 8 bold
Colour     constant 11
Colour     api 14
Colour     regex 14
Colour     punct 7
| --- what a JSScript program has ready to use (src/core/jsrun.js)
Complete   print(...values) Show values in the program's output window, on a line of their own
Complete   input(prompt) Ask for a line of text (use await): const name = await input('Name? ')
Complete   sleep(ms) Wait ms milliseconds without freezing the desktop (use await)
Complete   beep() Sound the bell
Complete   sound(channel, amplitude, pitch, duration) Play a note, like BASIC's SOUND
Complete   wimpColour(n) The CSS colour of Wimp colour n (0-15)
Complete   saveAs(opts) A Save box: { task, filename, filetype, getData, onSaved }
Complete   query(opts) A query box: { task, title, message, buttons } - resolves to the button's text
Complete   infoBox(task, info) An Info box: { name, purpose, author, version }
Complete   colourMenu(title, current, onPick) A menu of the 16 Wimp colours
Complete   Menu(title, items) A menu: new Menu('Title', [{ text, action, ticked, shaded, submenu, dotted }])
Complete   ctx.args The command tail the program was run with
Complete   ctx.argv The command tail split into words
Complete   ctx.file The program's own full name
Complete   ctx.dir The directory the program is in
| --- task: this program
Complete   task.createWindow(def) Make a window: { title, x, y, w, h, extent, flags, colours, workButton }
Complete   task.every(ms, fn) Call fn every ms milliseconds; returns a function that stops it
Complete   task.after(ms, fn) Call fn once, after ms milliseconds
Complete   task.animate(fn) Call fn before every screen refresh; returns a function that stops it
Complete   task.addIconbarIcon(spec) An icon on the icon bar: { sprite, text, onClick, menu, onDataLoad }
Complete   task.onMessage(type, fn) Handle a Wimp message such as 'Quit'
Complete   task.reportError(message) An error box from this program
Complete   task.quit() End the program: its windows, icons and timers go
Complete   task.name The program's name, as the Task Manager shows it
| --- windows (w = task.createWindow(...))
Complete   w.open() Open the window (on top)
Complete   w.close() Close the window (it can be opened again)
Complete   w.delete() Close the window for good
Complete   w.setTitle(text) Change the title bar
Complete   w.useCanvas(fn) Draw the window with fn(g, r): g is a canvas context, r the visible area
Complete   w.invalidate() Ask for the window to be redrawn
Complete   w.on(event, fn) Handle an event: 'click', 'key', 'close', 'pointermove', 'dataload' ...
Complete   w.setExtent(size) Set the work area size: { w, h }
Complete   w.scrollTo(x, y) Scroll the work area
Complete   w.icons The window's icons (w.icons[0] ...)
Complete   w.isOpen True while the window is open
| --- the Wimp
Complete   wimp.setCaret(w) Give window w the input focus, so it gets key presses
Complete   wimp.menus.openAt(menu, ev, opts) Open a menu where the mouse was clicked: { task }
Complete   wimp.width The screen's width in pixels
Complete   wimp.height The screen's height in pixels
Complete   wimp.beep() Sound the bell
| --- files
Complete   vfs.readText(path) Read a text file (use await)
Complete   vfs.readFile(path) Read a file's bytes (use await)
Complete   vfs.writeFile(path, data, opts) Write a file: opts { filetype: 0xFFF }
Complete   vfs.exists(path) True if the file or directory exists
Complete   vfs.list(dir) The objects in a directory: [{ name, path, type, filetype, size }]
Complete   vfs.stat(path) Information about a file, or null
Complete   vfs.mkdir(path) Make a directory
Complete   vfs.delete(path) Delete a file or empty directory
| --- the language's own objects
Complete   Math.random() A random number from 0 up to (not including) 1
Complete   Math.floor(x) x rounded down
Complete   Math.round(x) x rounded to the nearest whole number
Complete   Math.abs(x) x without its sign
Complete   Math.sqrt(x) The square root of x
Complete   Math.min(a, b) The smaller
Complete   Math.max(a, b) The larger
Complete   Math.sin(a) Sine of an angle in radians
Complete   Math.cos(a) Cosine of an angle in radians
Complete   Math.PI 3.14159...
Complete   JSON.stringify(value) Turn a value into text
Complete   JSON.parse(text) Turn text back into a value
Complete   Number(text) Turn text into a number (NaN if it isn't one)
Complete   String(value) Turn a value into text
| --- drawing on a window's canvas (w.useCanvas((g, r) => ...))
Complete   g.fillStyle The colour for filling: 'red', '#ff8800' or wimpColour(n)
Complete   g.strokeStyle The colour for lines
Complete   g.lineWidth The width of lines, in pixels
Complete   g.fillRect(x, y, w, h) Fill a rectangle
Complete   g.strokeRect(x, y, w, h) Draw a rectangle's outline
Complete   g.clearRect(x, y, w, h) Clear a rectangle
Complete   g.beginPath() Start a new shape
Complete   g.moveTo(x, y) Move the pen without drawing
Complete   g.lineTo(x, y) Draw a line to x, y
Complete   g.arc(x, y, r, start, end) An arc or circle (angles in radians)
Complete   g.closePath() Join the shape's end to its start
Complete   g.stroke() Draw the shape's outline
Complete   g.fill() Fill the shape
Complete   g.fillText(text, x, y) Draw text
Complete   g.font The font for text: '16px Homerton'
Complete   g.textAlign 'left', 'center' or 'right'
| --- strings and arrays (any name before the dot)
Complete   text.length The number of characters (or an array's items)
Complete   text.toUpperCase() The text in capitals
Complete   text.toLowerCase() The text in small letters
Complete   text.trim() The text without spaces at either end
Complete   text.split(separator) Split the text into an array
Complete   text.includes(part) True if the text (or array) contains it
Complete   text.padStart(n) The text with spaces in front, n characters long
Complete   text.padEnd(n) The text with spaces after it, n characters long
Complete   text.startsWith(part) True if the text starts with part
Complete   text.endsWith(part) True if the text ends with part
Complete   text.slice(start, end) Part of the text (or array)
Complete   number.toFixed(places) The number as text with that many decimal places
Complete   list.push(item) Add an item to the end of the array
Complete   list.pop() Take the last item off the array
Complete   list.join(separator) The items joined into text
Complete   list.sort(compare) Sort the array
Complete   list.indexOf(item) Where the item is (-1 if it isn't)
Complete   list.filter(test) The items test says yes to
Complete   list.map(fn) A new array of fn(item) for each item
Complete   list.forEach(fn) Call fn(item) for each item
